{
  "turn_number": 4,
  "player_text": "I leave the runner and step up to the nearest guard holding the line. I ask, calmly, what a traveler has to do to pass this gate.",
  "visible_motivation": "The runner quoted my own words back and said I would need another source. The guards are the people holding the choke point, so I ask them how to pass.",
  "intended_meaning": "Ask a gate guard what is required to pass the gate.",
  "generated_candidate": "\"I'm afraid I can't say for certain what a traveler must do to pass the gate,\" the tavern runner replies, voice low and wary, eyes flicking to the guards holding the line. \"Rules shift as fast as the rumors, and the guards follow orders that change with the day.\" They nod toward the gate serjeant overseeing the crowd. \"Your best bet is to speak directly with the serjeant or the captain. They decide who goes through, and what conditions must be met. But be prepared—and keep your business quiet.\"",
